            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HealthyFoodLvr"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe was so easy, and the onion rings tasted so good. Next time I'm going to try to stick dry mix on there first so that maybe when the onion rings are done frying there will be more breading left on the actual onion ring. Overall - Tasted Wonderful!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderful with a few minor modifications..... i ended up using 12 oz beer and enough milk to make a thinner batter as it was biscuit consistency without the added moisture. Also added about a tablespoon of seasoned salt in the mixture because it was so bland. I also put extra flour and seasoned salt in a gallon bag and shook the onion rings in it to coat them, then let them set on a plate about a half hour to dry out more before coating with the batter and frying then only a few at a time, not touching. They are wonderful and puffy, crispy, and the batter stayed on the rings just great! I'm definitely saving this recipe as my go-to onion ring batter!!! Next time i'll try with veggies :}",
            "datePublished": "2017-11-06T04:00:04.513Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mitzi Elena"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used to be hooked on Sonic onion rings, but I'm leaving all fast food and processed foods behind. My husband and I made these onion rings using sweet onions, and it's become our family favorite. I did add some extra beer because the batter is a bit thick. Thank you!",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-13T13:22:17.474Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MelissaAK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really easy and really tasty. I didn't feel the need to use any additional seasonings. If you want a little crunchier onion ring: batter it, coat it in corn meal, and then fry it.",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-04T22:12:50.303Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jodi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The first time I made it as directed but the batter seemed a little thick for my taste. I ended up adding more liquid. The second time I add less flour to start off with and they cooked up more evenly. Also, the recipe calls for salt and pepper to taste so I made the first onion ring and added more salt and pepper, it was a good way of doing it as to not get a super salty or over peppery ring.",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-18T00:57:34.683Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LivelyCow1858"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love the seasonings in the batter because they definitely give the rings a unique flavor. I did use a little more beer than the recipe called for as my batter was pretty thick, but next time I think I would use a whole can to make the batter even lighter and crispier.",
            "datePublished": "2025-05-11T15:16:25.142Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amanda"
            },
            "reviewBody": "YUM!! This batter was easy to make and actually stayed on the onions during and after frying. I used a whole bottle of Bar Harbor Blueberry beer and it gave it a really robust flavor. Batter was nice and thick too. Would definitely use again, but maybe using a fry daddy or something. I used just an inch or so of oil in a cast iron skillet. I'm thinking they'll do better if they're fully submurged in oil. Can't wait to try it on other veggies!!",
            "datePublished": "2011-10-20T04:56:35.443Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Abalicious"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is by far the best onion ring recipe out there. If you are looking for restaurant quality onion rings this is it. I just added some extra flavouring like a hint of chili, smoked paprika and onion powder. (Onion powder really enhances the onion flavour). I will be doing this again and again and again. :)",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-12T22:54:59.057Z"
          },
