            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DizzyStir9730"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I wish I had read some of the other reviews and could have improved on the recipe. As is, the batter was WAY too thick. I looked at other recipes and online and either the beer needs to be almost doubled or the flour cut in half. I fry fish perfectly all the time but when these cooked they came out doughy and not crispy. Also they were bland so hitting them with seasoned salt after cooking helped. By the end of the batch I wiped off enough batter on each ring that they started coming out pretty decent. I would almost double the beer and add way more seasoning. “Salt and pepper to taste” is impossible to gauge in a batter.",
            "datePublished": "2026-03-02T00:29:23.135Z"
